Z||000000||3fifty||02-12-2001||11:23 PM||||I have an 85 GT V6. Can I use a 160 degree<BR>thermostat without installing a different<BR>fan switch? If so,would it do any good with just the thermostat?<P>Thanks,<BR>350 one day!!!!!!!||||reg||10
Z||000001||FieroJoe||02-13-2001||10:33 AM||||The fan switch really isnt the issue here, it is the ECM always running the engine in "open-loop" mode, because the engine will never get hot enough for it to run normally.  You usually have to get a different PROM chip for the ECM.  Check out ogre's cave, the link is at the bottom of every forum page, he has a very nice article that goes in-dept with this subject.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
